From: TOBI Maintainers <tobi@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: permit read-only CID inspection on SD cards

TOBI must identify the exact card which supplied its recovery initramfs
before offering to overwrite that boot medium. A partition UUID cannot
identify cloned SD and eMMC images reliably. Permit reading the already
cached SD CID through the existing MMC register command. Keep the current
SD rejection for every other register, including CSD and EXT_CSD.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TOBI boot source identification]

diff --git a/cmd/mmc.c b/cmd/mmc.c
--- a/cmd/mmc.c
+++ b/cmd/mmc.c
@@ -1159,7 +1159,8 @@
 		return CMD_RET_FAILURE;
 	}
 
-	if (IS_SD(mmc)) {
+	/* CID is cached for both SD and eMMC; this read cannot alter media. */
+	if (IS_SD(mmc) && strcmp(argv[2], "cid")) {
 		printf("SD registers are not supported\n");
 		return CMD_RET_FAILURE;
 	}
